PR #2502  overall: bug_confirmed
Spec: Clarify that mstatus.TW traps WFI in all modes less privileged than M-mode (not just modes lower than the current privilege level), preventing guest/user code from evading WFI interception in virtualized or multi-level privilege environments
  [BUG] sys/riscv/include/riscvreg.h:82-134  (header — MSTATUS bit definitions)
      MSTATUS bit definitions cover UIE through SD (lines 82–118) but MSTATUS_TW (bit 21) is absent. HSTATUS_VTW (line 133) exists for the hypervisor extension, demonstrating awareness of the TW bit in the hstatus context, but the corresponding mstatus.TW constant is missing. Without this definition, the kernel has no vocabulary to read, check, clear, or handle mstatus.TW — it is structurally blind to the bit that causes WFI to trap as illegal instruction in S-mode.
